course: dictionary
lesson: 1608
title: Cheese: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cheese is a noun. It can mean a food, or one whole round block of it. Context tells you which one. In «There is no good evidence that cheese gives you nightmares», cheese means the food. In «Say cheese!», the word is part of a phrase that means smile for a photo.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Grated cheese» and «cheese on toast» show cheese as food you can eat. When you read «a cheese», the a tells you it is one whole block or one kind, not the food in general.
explain: Cheese is made when milk is thickened, or curdled, and the liquid is drained off. Some cheese-makers add acid to make the milk clump into lumps, as with soft paneer. Use what you know about a word to check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Cheese is a food made from milk. It can be yellow or white, and soft or hard.
fact: A cheese means one whole round block, or one particular kind of cheese.
fact: «Say cheese!» is a phrase people use before a photo, so everyone smiles.
fact: Cheese is a dairy food with calcium, which helps make bones and teeth strong.
fact: House mice mainly eat seeds, grain and crumbs; the cartoon idea that they love cheese above everything is not true.
exercise: «Say cheese!» is what people say before a photo. What does it ask everyone to do? | *Smile | Run away | Eat a snack | Close their eyes
exercise: In a fable by La Fontaine, Mr Crow is perched in a tree holding a cheese in his beak. What is in his beak? | *A cheese | A worm | A seed | A cake
exercise: «House mice mainly eat seeds, grain and crumbs.» What do house mice mainly eat? | Sugar and sweets | Only fish | *Seeds, grain and crumbs | Cheese above everything
test: Cheese is made from milk. Which of these is a kind of cheese? | Rice | *Paneer | Honey | Lemonade
test: «There is no good evidence that cheese gives you nightmares.» What does evidence mean here? | *Proof that something is true | A pet | A bad dream | A kind of cheese
exam: «Mlyntsi are thin pancakes eaten with jam or cottage cheese.» What are mlyntsi eaten with? | Nothing at all | *Jam or cottage cheese | Ice cream and chocolate | Milk only
